{"description":"GitHub issue maleolabs/eka-cli#27 (suggestion, low, source: agent, EKA 1.2.0): legal state transitions are discoverable only by hitting a transition refusal (e.g. scp draft-\u003eapproved refused with hint 'legal transitions from \"draft\": review'). The refusal message itself is excellent and deterministic; the gap is that the information arrives only AFTER a wasted call, forcing agents to trial-and-error each type's table (scp content-state vs plan planning-state differ).\n\nRevision 2 (2026-08-26, planning-time amendment): the deployed MCP surface has since evolved past the branch originally reviewed - it now includes a draft_read tool (with view retained as a deprecated alias). The v1 claim 'no draft_read exists' is corrected accordingly. The CORE GAP STANDS, re-verified live against the deployed server on 2026-08-26: the publish result observed this session carries exactly {schema, form, instanceVersion, objectHash, note} and the scaffold draftReport likewise carries NO state-table information - nothing exposes legal transitions proactively.\n\nStill-valid verified facts from source review:\n- Transition refusals are built in eka-core/runtime/transition.go - reason strings ('transition X -\u003e Y is not in the content-state table') plus unexported hint builders (legalTransitionsHint, legalPlanningTransitionsHint, legalContainerTransitionsHint, legalContentTransitionsHint) used exclusively for refusal hints; TransitionRefusal{Reason,Hint} envelope.\n- Building blocks already exported: conformance.DomainValues(domain, typeToken) and conformance.OwnedDomains(token) in eka-core/conformance/state.go - the single source of truth for ordered state values.\n\nFix direction (unchanged): surface legalTransitions (per owned state domain) in the MCP publish result, new-scaffold result, and draft-inspection output, computed from conformance.DomainValues - complementing, not replacing, the existing refusal hints. Turns a guaranteed-wasted call into zero calls.","acceptanceCriteria":"- MCP publish result report includes legalTransitions per owned state domain of the published type.\n- MCP new scaffold result (draftReport) includes legalTransitions for the scaffolded type, so lifecycle decisions happen at scaffold time.\n- If a draft-inspection surface exists on the tool boundary (draft_read and/or its deprecated alias), its output ALSO carries legalTransitions - that is the natural place an author looks before transitioning.\n- Values sourced exclusively from conformance.DomainValues / conformance.OwnedDomains (single source of truth) - no duplicated transition tables anywhere.\n- CLI parity considered: eka publish/new --json output carries the same field (follow-up acceptable if it complicates the human-readable output).\n- Tests pin the report shape for at least one content-state type (scp: draft-\u003ereview-\u003eapproved) and one planning-state type (plan: draft-\u003eapproved).\n- Review findings posted as a comment on maleolabs/eka-cli#27; issue closed only after the fix ships in a release."}